DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83171\nhttps://spanport.dartmouth.edu/news/2026/10/la-mirada-bori
 cua-exhibition-symposium\n\nDescription:\nImage -\nMiguel Luciano\,\nVultu
 re Brand Yams\n(2017).\nJoin us for Day 1 of La Mirada Boricua Symposium -
  View the Full Program\nHere\n.\nLa Mirada Boricua” translates as “The
  Boricua Gaze\,” with “Boricua” derived from the Taíno indigenous n
 ame for Puerto Ricans. La Mirada Boricua is a faculty exhibition curated
  by Professor Israel Reyes of the Department of Spanish and Portuguese and
  hosted by the Hood Museum that explores contemporary Puerto Rican art and
  the intimate and public spaces it creates for engaging with the archipela
 go’s colonial history\, the experience of migration and diaspora\, and t
 he possibilities for a decolonial future.\nLa Mirada Boricua events are sp
 onsored by The Department of Spanish & Portuguese\, The Leslie Center for 
 the Humanities\, and the Hood Museum of Art.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Lesli
 e Center for the Humanities\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWh
 y this was included: Free Food category\n\nFood availability is inferred f
