BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Neighbors – Closing Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T190000
DTSTAMP:20261104T183234Z
UID:dartmouth-83194@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83194\nhttps://studioart.dartmouth.edu/news/2026/09/faculty-exhib
 ition-chris-sollars-neighbors\nhttps://www.sevendaysvt.com/arts-culture/ar
 treview/screen-time-two-solo-art-shows-consider-a-new-era-of-tech/\n\nDesc
 ription:\nClosing Reception\nNov 7\, 2026 4PM - 7PM\nJoin Associate Profes
 sor of Studio Art Chris Sollars for snacks in the 0102 gallery\, Visual Ar
 ts Center. His faculty exhibition\, The Neighbors\, is on view Sept. 15 
 – Nov. 8.\nIn his first solo exhibition at Dartmouth College\, multidisc
 iplinary artist and Associate Professor of Studio Art Chris Sollars presen
 ts\nThe Neighbors\n\, a new body of work inspired by coexistence and inqui
 ry.\nSet in rural Vermont\, The Neighbors is a multimedia video installati
 on about the non-human inhabitants of the lands around the artist’s home
 . After over two decades living in San Francisco\, California\, Sollars mo
 ved to Vermont in the fall of 2024. To get to know his new home and neighb
 ors\, he has spent the past two years interacting with his surroundings th
 rough slow listening and observation\, learning them spatially and tempora
 lly.  This intentional gathering of information has taken the form of dia
 ristic snapshots taken throughout the seasons\, field recordings\, the col
 lection of discarded nests and materials\, and the placement of wildlife c
 ameras in the open woodland edges of his home\, which neighbors a land tru
 st\, a national forest\, and the Appalachian Trail.\nRead the\nreview\nof 
 The Neighbors Exhibition in Seven Days by Alice Dodge.\n\nSponsor / organi
 zer: Studio Art Department\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy
  this was included: Free Food category\; explicit food-service wording\; f
 ood keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferred from the
  source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T183234Z
LOCATION:0102 Gallery\, Visual Arts Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=83194
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
