BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film & Media Studies Colloquium with Technical Director Warren Coc
 kerham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T140000
DTSTAMP:20261104T183234Z
UID:dartmouth-83203@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83203\n\nDescription:\nJoin the Department of Film & Media Studie
 s for our fall colloquium with Technical Director\, Warren Cockerham.\nWar
 ren Cockerham is a filmmaker\, educater\, and cinema technologist. He rece
 vied his MFA from the School of the Art Institute of Chicago in 2010. His 
 early work in media access and advocacy led to the founding of FilmLAB@151
 2\, a film and video program for teenagers in Chicago's North Lawndale com
 munity.\nHis film work is driven by an interest in power structures within
  familial and intimate relationships\, and how those dynamics are shaped\,
  obscured\, or reframed through archival media–both public and private. 
 His projects tend to resist conventional narrative\, instead organizing th
 emselves around a set of problems or tensions. His work has screened at ve
 nues across the U.S. and internationally.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Film & M
 edia Studies Department\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy th
 is was included: Free Food category\n\nFood availability is inferred from 
 the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T183234Z
LOCATION:Loew Auditorium\, Black Family Visual Arts Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=83203
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
